{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>It is holy.</b> The meaning is its formulation — even if one makes it from unconsecrated ingredients, and one who makes it in its formulation is liable as though he offers up an elevation-offering and a sin-offering for himself. But if he made it in order to learn from it, or on condition to give it to the public, it is permitted. So they said in Karetot (5a)." "Further, it appears that the verse's saying <b>קֹדֶשׁ הוּא קֹדֶשׁ יִהְיֶה</b> may be understood in this manner: ״קֹדֶשׁ הוּא״ — this is the oil that Moses made, whose sanctity is greater, for one who anoints from it is liable to karet, as it says immediately afterward ״וַאֲשֶׁר יִתֵּן מִמֶּנּוּ״, and they said in Karetot (6a): ״מִמֶּנּוּ״ — meaning from the oil that Moses made, and not from anointing oil other than it. And the verse's saying <b>קֹדֶשׁ יִהְיֶה לָכֶם</b> — this is the oil of the generations, which is not equivalent to the sanctity of the oil of Moses, and one is liable only for compounding its like. And the word ״מִמֶּנּוּ״ alone would not suffice, for without it I would have said: until he anoints all of it." "And our Rabbis of blessed memory (Karetot 6a) derived from this verse that it must be made in a holy place. According to their words, He should have said this in His commandment, not in the warning of ״לֹא תַעֲשׂוּ כָּמוֹהוּ״. And their words, may their memory be for blessing, are nothing more than an asmakhta for laws transmitted orally, and our words are the plain sense of the verse."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:44.447782762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}